 "reading": "Skipping authentication removes 136,624 of 10,128,736 cycles (1.3%): merkle.auth 138,164 -> 893. prove_seconds 3.580 -> 3.663 s, shards 4 -> 4, peak GPU memory unchanged. The guest's cycles are statement machinery: parse.statement 3.71 M + merkle.table (opening-table construction, no hashing) 4.56 M = 82%; digest 0.90 M (9%); the relation (gates) 0.43 M (4.2%); leaf hashing + path folding 0.14 M (1.3%). The relation-only diagnostic (unsound-relation-only, r20260922-050349-3373 and two repeats) isolates the relation: 406,671 cycles (4.0% of the sound guest), of which gates 346,484 (the bare chain through GateSet::evaluate; the sound guest's 426,223 gates cycles include the interpreter's per-gate op resolution and argument gathering over the parsed statement), parse of the compact input 31,756, two sha256 digests 23,989, input read 363. Proving: 2 shards (sound: 4), prove_seconds 0.855 / 0.868 / 0.913 s over three proofs (sound 3.580 s, i.e. 4.1x), setup 15.9-16.0 s (sound 17.4 s), proof 2,799,064 B (sound 5,898,276 B), sampled peak GPU memory 7.7-9.9 GiB (sound 19.5 GiB). K=16 relation-only: 13,226 cycles, 2 shards, 0.680 s. The arithmetic baseline of the zkVM path at K=1536 is therefore ~0.87 s of GPU proving after a ~16 s key setup; the sound proof spends the other ~2.7 s on statement machinery, digest and authentication. Nothing here is a result: the relation-only guest verifies no statement."
